Hi All

Thanks once again for all the invaluable tips in getting
my 4100 working.

As it turned out I had alpha bios version 5.21 installed
on the machine, once I had upgraded the firmware it
all booted up just fine and is now being well and hammered
with a database load test, and all is looking good.

One interesting this is that I happen to have 2 of these
little beasties and the other one has not been upgraded
yet so I might have ago woth the serial console and post
the panic message to the archive, incase anybody else
has this problem.

On a side issue the two boxes used to be installed 
together in a rather nifty looking raid setup.

In all I have 33 disks (mostly taking up all the room
in my basement) and each 4100 has two of everything.

However it has a pretty fancy looking scsi adapter with a
label saying "A09-KZPSAPS".

Is this board supported under linux by any chance ? I've 
search about a bit but to no avail.

Off to play with my new machine !

--Jools




