Picking up src.rpm on www.tuxfinder.com and typing 'xine-' in search box
returned right away 25 references.  True, some of them are for
'xine-lib-' while other for 'xine-ui-'.  Are you saying that none of
this stuff compiles on Alpha?  If not with 'rpm --rebuild ...' then
maybe after some small tweaks?

Even when I asked for alpha.rpm I got that:

1 xine-lib-0.9.0-1.alpha.rpm
2 xine-lib-alsa-0.9.0-1.alpha.rpm
3 xine-lib-oss-0.9.0-1.alpha.rpm

All these are actually references to download particulars.  So at least
a source for _that_ should trivially recompile if it is not running
outright due to different shared library versions.

A coverage on www.tuxfinder.com is rather spotty but usually one
can find there at least a starting point for newer or more complete
stuff. :-)

